# Bite a giant rat to death and see whether the poison rider keeps hitting the
# corpse. This is the session for inc-upw.32.
#
#   INCURSION_RIDER_PROBE=1 tools/headless.sh tools/keys/rider-corpse.keys 1
#
# Read the result with tools/check_rider_corpse.sh, which is what asserts on
# the probe log. This file only produces the log.
#
# THE SCENARIO IS ARRANGED IN THE ENGINE, not here, because no key script can
# reach it: the wizard menu's polymorph and summon prompts are interactive
# glyph pickers that this key format cannot drive. With INCURSION_RIDER_PROBE
# set, Player::ChooseAction (src/Player.cpp) turns the player into a giant
# spider on his first action and stands a one-hit-point giant rat east of him.
# The spider's only attack is "A_BITE for 1d8 AD_PIERCE and AD_POIS (DC 16)",
# and the "and" clause is the A_ALSO rider whose loop this bead is about.
#
# So the whole script is RIGHT. The first bite that lands kills the rat, and
# the rider is thrown at whatever is left. The presses after the kill walk
# east over the corpse and cost nothing.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

# The shapeshift drops every carried weapon and says so, and the message pile
# opens a "-- more --" prompt that eats whatever key comes next. Clear it
# before the first attack, or all the RIGHTs are spent on the prompt.
SPACE*10

RIGHT*24

@dump:after-the-kill
@quit
